<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Admiral Peary is seen in the afternoon after his upper endoscopy and colonoscopy this morning. He has more energy, climbs a flight of stairs without stopping, and walks half a mile with his stick. The pins and needles in his feet are less, though the numbness at the ends of his feet remains. He has given himself three weekly injections without trouble. The blister on his left forefoot healed within two weeks; podiatry saw him twelve days ago, pared the callus and fitted extra-depth shoes with toe fillers. He started physical therapy three weeks ago. He has not fallen. The endoscopist reported pale, thin mucosa in the body of the stomach and a normal antrum, and no polyps in the colon; biopsies are pending. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Energy</td><td>Better; one flight of stairs without stopping</td></tr><tr><td>Feet</td><td>Less tingling; numbness at the ends persists; blister healed</td></tr><tr><td>Hemoglobin</td><td>12.0 g/dL; MCV 101 fL</td></tr><tr><td>Potassium</td><td>4.3 mmol/L</td></tr><tr><td>Endoscopy</td><td>Atrophic-looking body mucosa; antrum normal; biopsies pending</td></tr><tr><td>Colonoscopy</td><td>No polyps</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

